in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @io
in @labeled
in @peer

# @tool — the family-root for FIRST-ORDER TECH TOOL identity, version,
# contract, and provenance. Sibling of @io, @mirror, @kintsugi, @torus,
# @peer, @void, @fate, @spectral, @bauchladen, @autopoietic,
# @butterfly, @cybernetic/*.
#
# Landed 2026-07-18 as §8 forward-promise discharge of Mara's closure
# canonical spec `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-sentence.md`
# (§3.4 + §12.1). Substrate-decl'd this tick under `[substrate-floor:
# @io-boundary]` marker: this shard COMPOSES over existing @io/X
# mechanism adapters; no Rust extension authored. Per Alex 2026-07-14
# feedback `feedback_no_rust_extension_shortcut` + Alex 2026-07-16
# 8th-repetition feedback `feedback_detector_inadequacy_answer_is_
# never_rust`, the detector answer is NEVER Rust; @tool composes via
# shard-body over @io.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-
#   sentence.md` §3 (Mara `2dd8ddb`; §3.1 audit + §3.2 mint + §3.3
#   altitude split against @io + §3.4 species list + §3.5 parametric
#   shape).
# - Alex 2026-07-18 direct-transcript verbatim: "We might want a
#   @tool prism. Maybe." → "I was thinking that @tool is the wrapper
#   for any first-order tech tool on the planet." → "Yes, now you see
#   it. And then it becomes a wrapper for the type system:
#   `@tool(cargo ..)` `@tool(git ..)`. The @roomba probably discharges
#   into a sequence of @tool calls."
# - Recognition promotion #R-the-compiler-in-one-sentence (closure
#   spec §7 PROMOTED via Alex direct-transcript first-witness gate
#   close): the compiler IS a Fate-biased @roomba discharging @tool(X,
#   args) sequences over @io through fractal projections.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit (closure §3.1) ===
#
# Grep verdict clean at family-root altitude:
#
#   - `tool` word appears at `shards/mirror/lens/mcp.mirror:57` as an
#     ACTION verb (`tool(name, args: ref) -> mcp { \ }`) — MCP
#     server's own vocabulary for tool registration. DIFFERENT
#     ALTITUDE (MCP-facing) with DIFFERENT CARRIER (mcp vs
#     tool_invocation).
#   - `@tool` as family-root DOES NOT EXIST elsewhere. Verified via
#     grep across all `shards/*.mirror` and `docs/**/*.md`.
#
# Two altitudes co-exist admissibly per closure spec §16
# forward-promise 7 (two-tick collapse deferred). Readable-name-at-
# each-altitude first; foundational unification is a later decision.
#
# === What @tool IS ===
#
# The IDENTITY + VERSION + CONTRACT + PROVENANCE altitude for any
# first-order tech tool. WHICH tool, WHAT version, signed by WHOM,
# invoked WHERE, against WHAT nix-pin. Not the mechanism. Not the
# bytes-crossing-the-syscall-boundary. Those live at @io/X.
#
# @tool(X, args) is the substrate-decl'd wrapper the compiler
# reasons about BEFORE touching @io; @io/X.exec is the mechanism
# the wrapper discharges INTO at dispatch time.
#
# === What @tool is NOT ===
#
# 1. NOT the mechanism altitude. That's @io/X. Composition direction
#    is @tool(X, args) → @io/X.exec; NEVER the reverse.
# 2. NOT a species under @io. Different altitude → different family-
#    root. Per closure spec §3.3: composing over @io does not mean
#    collapsing into @io.
# 3. NOT the MCP action-verb `tool`. That's a JSON-RPC action at
#    @mirror/lens/mcp:57; different altitude, different carrier.
#    Two-tick collapse forward-promised.
# 4. NOT a Rust extension. This shard composes; no `.rs` authorship
#    beyond `prismqueer::void::LiquidVoid<ToolInvocation>` per
#    closure §5.4 (which is trait FLOOR, not extension).
# 5. NOT a package manager. @tool wraps INVOCATION; @spectral/garden
#    wraps DEPENDENCY-DECLARATION; siblings, not composed.
#
# === Composition direction (closure spec §3.3) ===
#
#   @tool(X, args)  ─dispatches─▶  @io/X.exec  ─crosses─▶  syscall
#         │                              │                      │
#     inference                     mechanism              actual bytes
#     altitude                      altitude               (outside world)
#         │                              │
#         └─ compiler reasons here ──────┘
#                                        │
#                        realisation discharges here
#
# The compiler NEVER reasons directly about @io/X.exec bytes; it
# reasons about @tool(X, args) invocations and lets @io discharge.
#
# === The 5-op prism inherits from @void (closure §10) ===
#
# Per `shards/void.mirror` §Composition inheritance: every family-
# root prism declaration `prism @X { focus/project/split/shift/settle
# X }` at family-root altitude IS the substrate-decl saying "this
# family inherits Void's basis." @tool's 5-op pattern below carries
# that inheritance; no `in @void` explicit import needed today per
# `shards/void.mirror` §Composition inheritance discipline.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   POSIX exec (1988)          the substrate ancestor of process
#                              invocation; @tool's `exec` action
#                              maps to POSIX exec at the @io/X
#                              boundary.
#   Cargo (Rust 2014)          per-tool subcommand grammar; @tool/
#                              cargo species specializes this.
#   Nix (Dolstra 2003)         content-addressed tool pinning;
#                              @tool.version_of + tools{} block +
#                              @tool/nix species compose this into
#                              the substrate.
#   BuildKit (Docker 2018)     content-addressed action cache with
#                              per-tool identity; sibling structural
#                              pattern at container altitude.
#   Bazel (Google 2015)        toolchain declaration + hermetic
#                              invocation; the tools{} block is
#                              structurally adjacent.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-
#               sentence.md` §3 + §4 + §12.1;
#               `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md`
#               (Mara, this tick; @tool/go + @tool/docker + @tool/
#               gitlab-ci as first cross-language species);
#               `docs/specs/roomba-substrate-walker-that-feeds-
#               kintsugi.md` (the @roomba consumer that emits
#               @tool sequences).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]],
#                      [[feedback-detector-inadequacy-answer-is-never-rust]],
#                      [[feedback-composition-primitive-naming-convention]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
# Recognition ancestry: #R-the-compiler-in-one-sentence (PROMOTED),
#                       #79 (5-op basis IS Void's tongue),
#                       #55 (form/process partition — @tool form-side,
#                       @io process-side),
#                       #98 candidate (content-addressing across scopes
#                       — @tool.version pins compose with the four
#                       existing witnesses).
# Related shards: io.mirror (mechanism altitude sibling),
#                 io/git.mirror (composed by @tool/git species),
#                 io/cargo.mirror (composed by @tool/cargo species),
#                 tool/cargo.mirror + tool/git.mirror +
#                 tool/nix.mirror (FLOOR species this tick),
#                 mirror/lens/mcp.mirror (co-altitude vocabulary,
#                 two-tick collapse forward-promised),
#                 void.mirror (5-op basis parent).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/tool.mirror`
# declares `@tool` and only that.

source @arxiv/exec/posix-1988
source @arxiv/build-systems/cargo-2014
source @arxiv/package-managers/dolstra-2003-nix

prism @tool {
  focus tool_invocation
  project tool_invocation
  split tool_invocation
  shift tool_invocation
  settle tool_invocation
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === The tool_id carrier ===
#
# Closed variant + `opaque(str)` escape hatch. Each concrete species
# (@tool/cargo, @tool/git, @tool/nix, ...) surfaces its own tag; the
# `opaque(str)` escape admits tools without substrate-decl'd species.
#
# Q2 (closure §15) held permissive: `opaque(str)` admissible at
# tools{} block level; substrate-honesty discipline reads: "consumers
# CAN escape, but the substrate NAMES the escape so it's visible."
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying tag.
type tool_id =
  | cargo             # @tool/cargo species (this tick)
  | git               # @tool/git species (this tick)
  | nix               # @tool/nix species (this tick)
  | ffmpeg            # forward-promised species
  | kubectl           # forward-promised species
  | docker            # forward-promised (StageFreight delivery, Mara this tick)
  | npm               # forward-promised species
  | pip               # forward-promised species
  | sqlite            # forward-promised species
  | curl              # forward-promised species
  | jq                # forward-promised species
  | go                # forward-promised (StageFreight delivery, Mara this tick)
  | gitlab_ci         # forward-promised (StageFreight delivery, Mara this tick)
  | opaque(str)       # escape hatch for tools without substrate-decl'd species

# === The tool_invocation carrier ===
#
# The typed record @tool(X, args) resolves to. Substrate-decl'd
# per closure spec §3.2. Every field carries typed provenance.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (tool_id, args, invoker,
# working_dir, env) tuple. `signature` and `version` are late-bound
# (resolved at dispatch); they do NOT contribute to identity for
# addressability but DO contribute for admissibility (per
# tool_invocation_admissible bilateral below).
type tool_invocation = {
  # X — the tool identity per tool_id variant
  tool_id: tool_id,
  # args — the tool's argument vector (structured, not opaque str)
  args: ref,
  # provenance — the substrate-decl'd witness of who invoked
  invoker: peer,
  # signature — the @trust chain's signature over (tool_id, args, invoker)
  # (forward-promised @trust family-root; carrier substrate-decl'd here)
  signature: ref,
  # version — the tool's version, resolved via @io/X.version or nix pin
  version: ref,
  # working_dir — the @io/fs cwd for the invocation
  working_dir: ref,
  # env — the @io/env variable set for the invocation
  env: ref,
}

# === The tool_result carrier ===
#
# The substrate-decl'd outcome of one @tool(X, args) call. The
# @io/X.exec discharge lifts to this shape at return-time.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (exit_code, stdout,
# stderr, duration, witness) tuple.
type tool_result = {
  exit_code: ref,     # int at species-refinement altitude
  stdout: ref,        # bytes at species-refinement altitude
  stderr: ref,        # bytes at species-refinement altitude
  duration: ref,      # duration at @epistemologic/reality/time altitude
  witness: ref,       # witnessed_run per @kintsugi/roomba
}

# === The tool_artifact carrier ===
#
# Per @labeled (recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED 2026-06-23): the
# deliverable tool-artifact is a labeled pair (tool_result,
# tool_invocation). Composes structurally with @io/oci's
# oci_artifact = labeled(ref, oci_manifest) and @io/git's
# git_artifact = labeled(git_object, git_ref_metadata).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the labeled pair.
type tool_artifact = labeled(tool_result, tool_invocation)

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === exec action — THE LOAD-BEARING dispatch ===
#
# Invoke the tool via @io/X.exec (mechanism altitude); returns
# tool_result at the substrate-decl'd contract level. The
# realisation discharges through the concrete @io/X species
# (@io/cargo, @io/git, @io/nix, ...) at the mechanism boundary.
#
# Composition direction (closure §3.3):
#   @tool.exec(invocation)
#     ─dispatches─▶ @io/<invocation.tool_id>.exec(args, env, cwd)
#       ─crosses─▶ syscall / actual process spawn
#
# Body discharges at species altitude per each @tool/<X> species'
# specialization. Family-root exec is the general dispatch surface.
exec(invocation: tool_invocation) -> tool { \ }

# === sign action — @trust chain integration ===
#
# The @trust chain signs the invocation BEFORE dispatch. Forward-
# promised @trust family-root (Mara territory next tick); this
# action names the substrate-decl surface the future @trust family
# lands into.
#
# Per closure spec §12.2 + §16 forward-promise 1: @trust family-root
# lands next Mara tick; this shard NAMES the composition point.
sign(invocation: tool_invocation, signer: peer) -> tool { \ }

# === verify action — @trust chain verification at dispatch ===
#
# The @trust chain verifies the invocation's signature at dispatch
# time. Companion to sign; both discharge through the forward-
# promised @trust family-root.
verify(invocation: tool_invocation) -> verdict { \ }

# === version_of action — nix/system pin resolution ===
#
# Resolve the version pin (nix or system) for a tool_id. Reads the
# tools{} block declared version pin (per @mirror/tools species
# grammar, forward-promised) OR discharges through @io/nix at the
# mechanism altitude to resolve the system-installed version.
#
# Body discharges at species altitude per each @tool/<X> species'
# specialization of version detection.
version_of(id: tool_id) -> ref { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilaterals
# ============================================================

# === tool_invocation_admissible composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at @tool altitude. Composes
# four sub-predicates:
#
#   1. invocation_well_formed(invocation, p) — tool_id resolves,
#      args are a valid vector, working_dir is a real ref
#   2. invocation_signed(invocation, p) — @trust chain signature
#      present and verifies
#   3. invocation_versioned(invocation, p) — version field pins to
#      a resolvable nix-pin or system-version
#   4. invocation_species_admissible(invocation, p) — the concrete
#      @tool/<X> species admits this specific invocation per its
#      species-decl bounds
#
# This is the Nth altitude lift of the composed-bilateral pattern
# per Mara @io/git.git_well_formed + Mara @io/oci.oci_well_formed +
# etc. The count is Mara-counted-from-brief; Pack-altitude
# verification deferred.
#
# Splinter-pole (honest): all four sub-predicates discharge; the
# invocation is well-formed AND signed AND version-resolved AND
# admissible per species.
# Narcissus-pole (deceptive): any one fails; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics (#57) distinguishes which sub-claim broke.
bilateral tool_invocation_admissible {
  sentinel "tool=invocation-well-formed-signed-versioned-admissible"
  arity    4
}

# === tool_result_witnessed composed bilateral ===
#
# The tool_result carries a valid witnessed_run — the @kintsugi/
# roomba discipline for content-addressed run-provenance.
#
# Splinter-pole: witness field carries a substrate-decl'd
# witnessed_run per @kintsugi/roomba conventions.
# Narcissus-pole: witness field is bare `ref` with no provenance
# chain, or the witness OID does not round-trip through
# @mirror/store.
bilateral tool_result_witnessed {
  sentinel "tool=result-carries-witnessed-run"
  arity    2
}

# ============================================================
# §5 The parametric shape `@tool(X, args)`
# ============================================================
#
# `@tool(X, args)` is NOT a new grammar form. It's the substrate-
# decl shorthand for a `tool_invocation` value where:
#
#   - X binds to `tool_id` (a substrate-decl'd variant tag or
#     opaque str)
#   - args binds to `list(str)` (the tool's argument vector)
#
# Consumers write `@tool(cargo, [check, --workspace])` and the
# substrate reads that as:
#
#   tool_invocation {
#     tool_id:     cargo,
#     args:        ["check", "--workspace"],
#     invoker:     <current-peer>,
#     signature:   <resolved-at-dispatch>,
#     version:     <resolved-via-@tool/cargo.version_of>,
#     working_dir: <resolved-via-cwd>,
#     env:         <resolved-via-env-substrate-decl>,
#   }
#
# The parametric surface IS the wrapper. The wrapper IS the type.
# The type IS what the compiler reasons about before touching @io.
#
# Q1 (closure §15) held parametric-shorthand form per Alex verbatim
# ("`@tool(cargo ..)` `@tool(git ..)`"). Species-form (`@tool/
# cargo(args)`) co-exists at species altitude but is NOT the
# canonical consumer-facing surface.

# ============================================================
# §6 Naming convention (closure §8)
# ============================================================
#
# Per `feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention` (Alex
# 2026-07-18 ratified): value-type generalizations follow
# `<primitive>_of_<input-shape>` with const-declared finite-set +
# ALL array.
#
# Application at @tool altitude:
#
#   - tool_of_id_args           the parametric shape @tool(X, args)
#   - exec_of_tool_invocation   the exec action per tool_id variant
#   - sign_of_tool_invocation   the @trust sign action per invocation
#   - verify_of_tool_signature  the @trust verify action per signature
#
# The primitive is @tool; the input-shape is the parametric binding
# (X, args); the finite-set is the tool_id closed variant + opaque
# (str) escape hatch; the ALL array is [cargo, git, nix, ffmpeg,
# kubectl, docker, npm, pip, sqlite, curl, jq, go, gitlab_ci]
# (all substrate-decl'd species; extensible via mint).
#
# Delightfully boring naming. No metaphor. No allusion. @tool is a
# tool. @tool(X, args) is a tool invocation. tool_result is what
# comes back. Every word means what it says.

# ============================================================
# §7 Forward-promised
# ============================================================
#
# Not landed this tick; named for future ticks:
#
# 1. @trust family-root (Mara territory next tick) — the crypto
#    floor's substrate-decl. Composes with @tool's `signature` field
#    + fractal::signature module. `tool.sign` + `tool.verify`
#    discharge through @trust at that altitude.
# 2. Additional @tool species as consumers pin them (@tool/ffmpeg,
#    @tool/kubectl, @tool/npm, @tool/pip, @tool/sqlite, @tool/curl,
#    @tool/jq, @tool/go, @tool/docker, @tool/gitlab-ci).
#    @tool/go + @tool/docker + @tool/gitlab-ci minted at
#    `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md` §3 (Mara this
#    tick); shard-decl files forward-promised for StageFreight
#    delivery arc.
# 3. Two-tick collapse of @mirror/lens/mcp's `tool` action-verb
#    into @tool family-root — currently co-exist at different
#    altitudes per closure §16 forward-promise 7.
# 4. `~bin` sigil canonical mint — the lens-over-@io/file escape
#    hatch that replaces `opaque(str)` at consumer-facing altitude.
#    Alex 2026-07-18 direct-transcript verbatim (Q2 answer):
#    "screams for a lens over the @io/file ~file sigil. ~bin".
#    Precedent: `~git'...'` sigil at `docs/specs/spectral-garden-
#    git-package-manager.md` §2.2. Forward-promised shard/species
#    location TBD (likely `shards/optics/lens/bin.mirror` sibling
#    to `shards/optics/lens/diff.mirror`).

out @tool
out tool_id
out tool_invocation
out tool_result
out tool_artifact
out exec
out sign
out verify
out version_of
out tool_invocation_admissible
out tool_result_witnessed
